`[Glassdoor confirmed: "What is the process of training transformers — supervised finetuning, RL involved?"]

TODO — key stages:
1. Pretraining — next-token prediction on massive web corpus (trillions of tokens)
2. SFT (Supervised Fine-Tuning) — teacher-forcing on (prompt, demonstration) pairs
3. Reward Modeling — train RM on human preference pairs (Bradley-Terry model)
4. RLHF via PPO — maximize E[r(x,y)] − β·KL(π || π_ref), KL prevents reward hacking
   OR DPO — eliminates explicit RM; direct loss on (prompt, chosen, rejected) triples
5. Evaluation — benchmarks (MMLU, HumanEval…) + red-teaming + human evals`
