    question: "What is LoRA? How does it work and when do you prefer it over full fine-tuning?",
    answer:
`TODO — key points:
• Low-Rank Adaptation: freeze base model, inject ΔW = A·B into weight matrices (A ∈ R^{d×r}, B ∈ R^{r×k}, r << min(d,k))
• Initialize A ~ N(0,σ), B = 0 so ΔW = 0 at start
• During forward: h = W₀x + (α/r)·BAx
• Typical r=8-64; reduces trainable params by 100–1000×
• Use when: limited GPU memory, multiple task adapters, fast iteration
• QLoRA: quantize base to 4-bit + LoRA on top; enables fine-tuning 70B on a single A100`
